Subject: The unit can ask where a property lives in a shape

What this does
  - `qjs_aot_shape_slot(shape, atom, &off)` (exported to the units, declared in quickjs-aot-rt.h) returns 1 and the byte offset of the property's slot in the object's property array when `atom` is an own data property of `shape`, else 0 (absent, accessor, variable reference, auto-initialised).

Why we need it
  A compiled copy of a callee inside a switch arm knows its receiver's shape (the arm's guard proved it), so its `this.f` reads can be a slot load at an offset computed from the shape, with no test, instead of a walk of the callee's own inline cache, which a copy never fills.
  The offsets are resolved once per cache epoch when the arm is first entered.

Soundness
  It reads only the shape. The unit keeps the answer while the shape cannot be freed or edited in place (`shape_free_epoch`, 0420) and the properties of its prototypes cannot change (`aot_pic_epoch`); an own data property's slot index is fixed for a shape's lifetime.

Functions touched
  `qjs_aot_shape_slot` (new).

No.

--- a/quickjs-aot-rt.h
+++ b/quickjs-aot-rt.h
@@ -229,0 +230,2 @@
+/* the byte offset of the own data property `atom` in objects of `shape`, or 0 when it is not one (a compiled copy resolves its receiver's slots from the shape) */
+QJS_AOT_STUB int qjs_aot_shape_slot(const void *shape, uint32_t atom, uint32_t *off);
--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -65255,0 +65256,28 @@
+}
+
+/* Where the property `atom` lives in objects of shape `shape`: 1 with the byte offset of its slot in the property array when it is an own
+   data property of the shape (an accessor, a variable reference or an auto-initialised slot is not), else 0. Reads nothing but the shape,
+   so it is only as good as the shape is: the caller keeps the answer while the shape cannot be freed or edited in place (shape_free_epoch)
+   and the properties of its prototypes cannot change (aot_pic_epoch). */
+QJS_AOT_STUB int qjs_aot_shape_slot(const void *shape, uint32_t atom, uint32_t *off)
+{
+    JSShape *sh = (JSShape *)shape;
+    JSShapeProperty *pr, *prop;
+    intptr_t h;
+
+    if (sh == NULL)
+        return 0;
+    h = (uintptr_t)atom & sh->prop_hash_mask;
+    h = prop_hash_end(sh)[-h - 1];
+    prop = get_shape_prop(sh);
+    while (h) {
+        pr = &prop[h - 1];
+        if (pr->atom == (JSAtom)atom) {
+            if ((pr->flags & JS_PROP_TMASK) != JS_PROP_NORMAL)
+                return 0;
+            *off = (uint32_t)((pr - prop) * sizeof(JSProperty));
+            return 1;
+        }
+        h = pr->hash_next;
+    }
+    return 0;
